INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'sbi-security-officer-60-posts-20261104', 'global', 'India',
'SBI Security Officer Recruitment 2026: 60 Posts for Military and Paramilitary Officers, Apply by 25 November',
'',
'State Bank of India has opened 60 Specialist Cadre Officer posts for serving and former military and paramilitary officers, with applications from 4 November 2026 to 25 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>State Bank of India has opened SBI security officer recruitment 2026 for 60 Specialist Cadre Officer posts, with online applications running from 4 November 2026 to 25 November 2026, the bank said in Advertisement No. CRPD/SCO/2026-27/28, dated 4 November 2026. SBI security officer recruitment 2026 covers two posts on a regular basis: Manager (Security) in Middle Management Grade Scale III and Deputy Manager (Security) in Middle Management Grade Scale II. The 60 vacancies are provisional, and the notification gives a combined total only, with no separate count for each post.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Advertisement</th><td>CRPD/SCO/2026-27/28, dated 4 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Posts</th><td>Manager (Security), MMGS-III; Deputy Manager (Security), MMGS-II</td></tr>
<tr><th>Total vacancies</th><td>60 (provisional, combined for both posts)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application window</th><td>4 November 2026 to 25 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Age limit</th><td>25 to 40 years as on 31 October 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Manager starting basic pay</th><td>Rs. 85,920 (scale Rs. 85,920 to Rs. 1,05,820)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Deputy Manager starting basic pay</th><td>Rs. 64,820 (scale Rs. 64,820 to Rs. 93,960)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application fee</th><td>Rs. 750 for UR, EWS and OBC; nil for SC and ST</td></tr>
<tr><th>Selection</th><td>Online written test followed by an interview</td></tr>
<tr><th>Posting</th><td>Anywhere in India, as per the bank's requirements</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>SBI security officer recruitment 2026: who can apply</h2>
<p>Read the eligibility rule first, because it excludes most graduates. SBI security officer recruitment 2026 is open only to candidates with qualifying service as officers in the armed forces or paramilitary forces. A degree on its own does not meet the requirement, and the bank states plainly that graduation without the prescribed service experience does not establish eligibility. Applicants must hold a degree in any discipline from a government-recognised university or institution, and must also meet the rank, service and medical conditions as on 31 October 2026.</p>
<p>For Manager (Security), the bank asks for an officer not below the rank of Major in the Indian Army, or the equivalent rank in the Navy or Air Force, with at least 10 years of commissioned service; or an officer not below the rank of Deputy Commandant in a paramilitary force, with at least 10 years of service as an officer in the force. For Deputy Manager (Security), the requirement is an officer not below the rank of Captain in the Army, or the equivalent in the Navy or Air Force, with at least 5 years of commissioned service; or an officer not below the rank of Assistant Commandant in a paramilitary force, with at least 5 years of service as an officer. Medical fitness in SHAPE-1 or an equivalent category is also required as on the date of the advertisement. Retired candidates must upload the medical category details from their discharge book or service record, while serving candidates must upload their latest Medical Board document.</p>
<p>The age limit for both posts is 25 to 40 years as on 31 October 2026, with upper-age relaxation for eligible reserved categories under Government of India guidelines. The category-wise split of the 60 vacancies is 25 for unreserved candidates, 16 for OBC, 9 for SC, 6 for EWS and 4 for ST.</p>
<h2>SBI security officer recruitment 2026: pay and probation</h2>
<p>The starting basic pay is Rs. 85,920 a month for Manager (Security), on a scale running to Rs. 1,05,820, and Rs. 64,820 a month for Deputy Manager (Security), on a scale running to Rs. 93,960. Those figures are basic pay scales, not guaranteed in-hand salaries: allowances, provident fund, National Pension System membership and medical facilities apply under SBI rules, and actual monthly earnings will depend on posting and deductions. The probation period for both posts is six months.</p>
<h2>SBI security officer recruitment 2026: selection and exam pattern</h2>
<p>Selection is through an online written test followed by a personal interview. The written test carries 200 objective questions for 200 marks over two hours: reasoning ability (50 questions, 25 marks, 30 minutes), English language (50 questions, 50 marks, 30 minutes), general awareness (50 questions, 25 marks, 25 minutes) and professional knowledge (50 questions, 100 marks, 35 minutes). The first three sections are qualifying in nature and their marks do not count towards final merit; only professional knowledge marks, together with the interview, decide the merit list. There is no negative marking for incorrect answers. The interview carries 100 marks, and the final merit calculation gives 70 per cent weight to professional knowledge and 30 per cent to the interview. Where candidates tie at the cut-off point, the bank will rank them by age in descending order. Annexure I of the notification sets out the full professional knowledge syllabus, covering security fundamentals, risk assessment, fire safety, CCTV, disaster management and bank security, so applicants should read it rather than rely on a summary.</p>
<p>The bank has published only a tentative schedule for the later stages: admit cards in December 2026, the online written examination in December 2026 or January 2027, interviews in January or February 2027, and the final result in February 2027. Exact dates will be announced through the SBI Careers website, and the bank may change the process to shortlisting followed by interview if required. Applicants should therefore check the official careers page and their registered email addresses for updates, rather than treating the tentative months as fixed dates.</p>
<h2>How to apply for SBI security officer recruitment 2026</h2>
<p>Apply online only, through the <a href="https://sbi.bank.in/web/careers/current-openings">SBI Careers portal</a>, between 4 November 2026 and 25 November 2026. Find Advertisement No. CRPD/SCO/2026-27/28 on the careers page and use its dedicated Apply Online link. The application fee is Rs. 750 for UR, EWS and OBC candidates and nil for SC and ST candidates, payable online, and registration is complete only after the fee has been paid on or before 25 November 2026. The fee is non-refundable. Readers tracking other openings should also note the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/indian-bank-apprentice-1500-posts-20261104">Indian Bank apprentice recruitment for 1,500 posts</a>, the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/rrc-central-railway-act-apprentice-2861-posts-20261104">Central Railway apprentice recruitment for 2,861 slots</a> and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/hcl-malanjkhand-trade-apprentice-171-posts-20261104">HCL Malanjkhand trade apprentice recruitment for 171 seats</a>. Keep service records, medical category documents and category certificates ready before starting, since the bank states that applications without the prescribed documents may not be considered, and check every entry before submitting.</p>
<p>Two warnings matter for this recruitment. First, apply only through the official SBI Careers portal and pay only through its gateway; SBI does not appoint agents, and any message asking for payment outside the portal, or promising selection, should be treated as fraud. Second, do not assume eligibility from the degree alone: service rank, years of service and the SHAPE-1 medical category are all conditions of this recruitment, and a candidate found ineligible at document verification will be removed even after clearing the test.</p>
<p><small>Sources: State Bank of India, Advertisement No. CRPD/SCO/2026-27/28, dated 4 November 2026, as summarised by FreeJobAlert; SBI Careers portal, sbi.bank.in.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/sbi-manager-security-deputy-manager-security-recruitment-2026-3078308','https://sbi.bank.in/web/careers/current-openings'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'rrc-central-railway-act-apprentice-2861-posts-20261104', 'global', 'India',
'Central Railway Apprentice Recruitment 2026: 2,861 Act Apprentice Slots, Apply by 2 December',
'',
'Railway Recruitment Cell, Central Railway has opened 2,861 Act Apprentice training slots across five clusters, with applications from 3 November 2026 to 2 December 2026 at 5:00 PM.',
'',
$$<p>Railway Recruitment Cell, Central Railway has opened Central Railway apprentice recruitment 2026 for 2,861 Act Apprentice training slots, with online applications running from 3 November 2026 at 11:00 AM to 2 December 2026 at 5:00 PM, the cell said in Notification No. RRC/CR/AA/2026, dated 3 November 2026. Central Railway apprentice recruitment 2026 covers five clusters: Mumbai with 1,712 slots, Bhusawal with 500, Pune with 271, Nagpur with 221 and Solapur with 157. The slots are provisional and may increase or decrease depending on Central Railway's administrative requirements, and the notified totals already include PwBD and ex-servicemen slots, which must not be added separately.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Notification</th><td>RRC/CR/AA/2026, dated 3 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Training slots</th><td>2,861 Act Apprentice slots, across five clusters</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application window</th><td>3 November 2026, 11:00 AM to 2 December 2026, 5:00 PM</td></tr>
<tr><th>Qualification</th><td>Class 10 with at least 50% aggregate marks, plus an NCVT/SCVT ITI certificate in the notified trade</td></tr>
<tr><th>Age limit</th><td>15 to 24 years as on 3 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Monthly stipend</th><td>Rs. 9,600 during one year of training</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application fee</th><td>Rs. 100; SC, ST, PwBD and women candidates exempt</td></tr>
<tr><th>Selection</th><td>Merit list from Class 10 and ITI marks; no written examination or interview</td></tr>
<tr><th>Merit list date</th><td>Not announced yet</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>Central Railway apprentice recruitment 2026: who can apply</h2>
<p>Central Railway apprentice recruitment 2026 is for ITI-trained candidates, and two restrictions at the top of the notification decide many applications before they start. First, a Class 10 pass alone is not enough: applicants must have passed Class 10 with at least 50 per cent aggregate marks from a recognised board and hold a National Trade Certificate, or a provisional certificate, in the relevant ITI trade issued by NCVT or SCVT. Second, engineering graduates and diploma holders are not eligible under this notification at all, since they are covered by a separate apprenticeship scheme, and candidates who are currently undergoing apprenticeship training, or who have already completed it, should not apply. Applicants must choose only one cluster, and must make sure their ITI trade has training slots available in the units of that cluster.</p>
<p>The age limit is 15 to 24 years as on 3 November 2026, with upper-age relaxation of 5 years for SC and ST candidates, 3 years for OBC candidates and 10 years for PwBD candidates, and separate conditions for ex-servicemen set out in the notification. The notification gives date-of-birth ranges for each category: 3 November 2002 to 3 November 2011 for general candidates, 3 November 1999 to 3 November 2011 for OBC candidates, and 3 November 1997 to 3 November 2011 for SC and ST candidates, with both dates inclusive. The trades on offer span mechanical, electrical, engineering, computer, communication and other designated trades, including fitter, electrician, welder, carpenter, machinist, turner, mechanic diesel, mechanic motor vehicle, electronics mechanic, instrument mechanic, computer operator and programming assistant, painter, sheet metal worker, mason, blacksmith, pipe fitter and plumber, cable jointer, wireman and stenographer, but not every trade is available in every cluster or workshop, so the trade-wise and unit-wise tables on pages 5 to 15 of the notification must be checked before choosing preferences.</p>
<h2>Central Railway apprentice recruitment 2026: clusters, stipend and training terms</h2>
<p>Mumbai holds well over half the slots, and its largest units are Matunga Workshop with 547 slots, Parel Workshop with 272 and Carriage and Wagon (Coaching) at Wadi Bunder with 258. Bhusawal's 500 slots include Carriage and Wagon Depot with 122 and Electric Locomotive Workshop with 118. Pune's 271 slots are led by Diesel Loco Shed with 121, while Nagpur's 221 include Carriage and Wagon Depot with 54, and Solapur's 157 include Kurduwadi Workshop with 56. Selected apprentices will train for one year at the chosen Central Railway unit or workshop, and will receive a monthly stipend of Rs. 9,600, as specified under Railway Board letter RBE No. 116/2025 dated 11 November 2025. That figure is the notified apprenticeship stipend, not the basic salary of a permanent railway employee, and hostel accommodation is not provided, so selected candidates must arrange their own accommodation during training.</p>
<p>The training terms carry a clear limit that applicants should understand before applying. This is apprenticeship training under the Apprentices Act, 1961, not permanent railway employment, and completing the training does not guarantee a job or automatic absorption into railway service; the railway administration is not obliged to offer a permanent post afterwards. Selected candidates must enter into a Contract of Apprenticeship Training before the programme begins, and for selected applicants who are minors, the contract must be entered into by their guardian. Document verification and training commencement dates have not been announced yet.</p>
<h2>Central Railway apprentice recruitment 2026: selection and how to apply</h2>
<p>There is no written examination and no interview. Selection rests on a merit list calculated from the simple average of Class 10 percentage marks and ITI percentage marks, followed by document verification and a medical fitness check. Applicants should therefore enter both sets of marks exactly as they appear on their certificates, without rounding or estimating. The application fee is Rs. 100 for candidates who are not covered by the notified exemptions, while SC, ST, PwBD and women candidates are exempt, and payment is made online by debit card, credit card, internet banking, UPI or wallet through the integrated payment gateway. The fee is non-refundable, and the cell advises candidates whose payment is deducted without confirmation to use the Verify Payment option and check the original transaction before paying again, since duplicate payments may not be refunded.</p>
<p>Apply online only, through the official Railway Recruitment Cell, Central Railway website at <a href="https://www.rrccr.com">rrccr.com</a>, before 5:00 PM on 2 December 2026. Applications sent by post or any other offline method will not be accepted. Open the notification, confirm the chosen trade is notified for the chosen unit, apply for one cluster only, and keep the confirmation for document verification. Apply only through rrccr.com and pay only through its official gateway: no agent can secure a slot, and any message asking for money beyond the notified fee, or promising a place on the merit list, should be treated as fraud. Readers comparing apprentice openings should also read the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/hcl-malanjkhand-trade-apprentice-171-posts-20261104">HCL Malanjkhand trade apprentice recruitment for 171 seats</a>, which uses a different merit formula and a two-step registration, and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/indian-bank-apprentice-1500-posts-20261104">Indian Bank apprentice recruitment for 1,500 posts</a>, which is a 12-month bank training programme rather than railway workshop training. The bank's regular officer opening published alongside this story, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/sbi-security-officer-60-posts-20261104">SBI security officer recruitment for 60 posts</a>, is a different kind of opportunity altogether, open only to serving or former military and paramilitary officers.</p>
<p><small>Sources: Railway Recruitment Cell, Central Railway, Notification No. RRC/CR/AA/2026, dated 3 November 2026, as summarised by FreeJobAlert; official website, rrccr.com.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/rrc-central-railway-act-apprentice-recruitment-2026-3078343','https://www.rrccr.com'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'hcl-malanjkhand-trade-apprentice-171-posts-20261104', 'global', 'India',
'HCL Trade Apprentice Recruitment 2026: 171 Seats at Malanjkhand, Apply by 24 November',
'',
'Hindustan Copper Limited has opened 171 Trade Apprentice seats at its Malanjkhand Copper Project, with applications from 5 November 2026 to 24 November 2026 and a merit list on 8 December 2026.',
'',
$$<p>Hindustan Copper Limited has opened HCL trade apprentice recruitment 2026 for 171 Trade Apprentice seats at its Malanjkhand Copper Project in Balaghat district, Madhya Pradesh, with online applications running from 5 November 2026 to 24 November 2026, the company said in Notification No. HCL/MCP/HR/Trade App./01/2026, dated 3 November 2026. HCL trade apprentice recruitment 2026 covers 19 technical and mining trades under the Apprentices Act, 1961, at a Miniratna Category-I Central Public Sector Enterprise under the Ministry of Mines. The merit list of shortlisted candidates is scheduled for publication on 8 December 2026, and the cut-off date for age and educational eligibility is 1 November 2026.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Notification</th><td>HCL/MCP/HR/Trade App./01/2026, dated 3 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Project</th><td>Malanjkhand Copper Project, Balaghat, Madhya Pradesh</td></tr>
<tr><th>Training seats</th><td>171, across 19 trades</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application window</th><td>5 November 2026 to 24 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Eligibility cut-off</th><td>1 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Age limit</th><td>18 to 25 years as on 1 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Training duration</th><td>1 year to 3 years, trade-wise</td></tr>
<tr><th>Stipend</th><td>As per Apprentices Act, 1961 norms; no figure stated in the summary checked</td></tr>
<tr><th>Merit list</th><td>8 December 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Selection</th><td>Academic and technical merit only; no written examination or interview</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>HCL trade apprentice recruitment 2026: trades and seats</h2>
<p>Electrician holds the largest share of HCL trade apprentice recruitment 2026, with 36 seats, followed by Computer Assistant (COPA) with 20 seats, and fitter, turner and machinist, and welder (gas and electric) with 16 seats each. Shotfirer and blaster (mines) holds 13 seats, mechanic diesel and instrument mechanic hold 10 each, and driver-cum-mechanic (light motor vehicle) holds 6 seats. Mate mines (fresher) and solar technician (electrician) hold 4 seats each, while draughtsman mechanical, surveyor, carpenter and plumber hold 3 each, and draughtsman civil, air conditioning and refrigeration mechanic, mason (building constructor) and horticulture assistant hold 2 each. The category-wise totals are 71 seats for unreserved candidates, 46 for OBC, 25 for SC, 17 for EWS and 12 for ST, adding to 171. Training runs for one year in most trades, for 3 years in mate mines (fresher), for 2 years in shotfirer and blaster, and for 1 year and 3 months in driver-cum-mechanic, so applicants should check the duration of their own trade before applying.</p>
<h2>HCL trade apprentice recruitment 2026: who can apply</h2>
<p>For the two mining fresher trades, mate mines and shotfirer and blaster, a Class 10 or matriculation pass under the 10+2 system is enough, and no ITI qualification is required. For the other 17 trades, applicants must have passed Class 10 and hold an ITI pass certificate in the respective designated trade from a recognised technical institute, under NCVT or SCVT. Where Class 10 results use CGPA grading, candidates must convert the CGPA into a percentage by multiplying by 9.5. Two exclusions deserve attention. Candidates holding higher professional qualifications such as a diploma or a B.E. or B.Tech degree will not be considered, and higher general degrees such as a B.A., B.Sc. or B.Com carry no additional weight. Candidates who passed ITI in 2025 or earlier must also submit an affidavit on non-judicial stamp paper, sworn before a magistrate or notary public, certifying that they have not undergone apprenticeship training or taken regular employment anywhere.</p>
<p>The age limit is 18 to 25 years as on 1 November 2026, with relaxation of 5 years for SC and ST candidates, taking the upper limit to 30 years, and 3 years for OBC (non-creamy layer) candidates, taking it to 28 years. Selection is made entirely on academic and technical merit, with no written examination and no interview. For ITI trades, the merit score gives 70 per cent weight to Class 10 board examination marks and 30 per cent to the relevant ITI trade marks. For the two non-ITI mining trades, the score rests entirely on Class 10 marks. Where two or more candidates obtain equal aggregate marks, the older candidate ranks higher, and final engagement remains subject to being declared medically fit under HCL medical fitness standards.</p>
<h2>How to apply for HCL trade apprentice recruitment 2026</h2>
<p>Applications require two mandatory steps, and completing only one of them is not enough. First, register on the National Apprenticeship Promotion Scheme portal at <a href="https://www.apprenticeshipindia.gov.in">apprenticeshipindia.gov.in</a>: register as a candidate, complete the profile to 100 per cent Aadhaar verification, update bank account details and complete eKYC, enter academic qualifications, search the establishment list for Hindustan Copper Limited, Malanjkhand Copper Project, and apply for the relevant trade opportunity, then note the apprenticeship registration number. Second, submit the application on the HCL portal at <a href="https://www.hindustancopper.com">hindustancopper.com</a>, in the Career section, under "Engagement of Trade Apprentices in MCP - 2026": enter the apprenticeship registration number and personal details, upload a recent colour passport-size photograph and a signature in black ink, each in JPG format and under 50 KB, and, for ITI passouts from 2025 or earlier, the notarised affidavit in PDF format under 1 MB. The "One Applicant - One Application" rule applies, so check every entry before submitting, and print the computer-generated application form and acknowledgement slip for document verification.</p>
<p>Apply well before 24 November 2026, since both registrations must be complete by the closing date, and keep the acknowledgement slip safe until the merit list appears on 8 December 2026. Apply only through the two official portals named above and pay no fee to any intermediary: HCL does not appoint agents for apprentice engagement, and any message asking for money to secure a seat should be treated as fraud. Note also that this is apprenticeship training under the Apprentices Act, 1961, not a permanent post, and the stipend figure is not stated numerically in the summary checked, only as per the Apprentices Act norms, so applicants should confirm the applicable stipend in the full notification before treating any figure quoted elsewhere as final. Readers comparing apprentice openings should also read the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/rrc-central-railway-act-apprentice-2861-posts-20261104">Central Railway apprentice recruitment for 2,861 slots</a>, which pays a stated stipend of Rs. 9,600 a month and selects on a simple average of Class 10 and ITI marks, and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/indian-bank-apprentice-1500-posts-20261104">Indian Bank apprentice recruitment for 1,500 posts</a>, a 12-month bank training programme. The regular officer opening published alongside this story, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/sbi-security-officer-60-posts-20261104">SBI security officer recruitment for 60 posts</a>, sits at the other end of the market, open only to serving or former military and paramilitary officers.</p>
<p><small>Sources: Hindustan Copper Limited, Notification No. HCL/MCP/HR/Trade App./01/2026, dated 3 November 2026, as summarised by PlacementStore; official portals, hindustancopper.com and apprenticeshipindia.gov.in. The summary used states that it has not been independently verified against the latest official notification, so applicants should confirm details in the full notification.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.placementstore.com/hcl-trade-apprentice-recruitment-2026-for-171-posts-apply-online-start-from-5-nov/','https://www.hindustancopper.com','https://www.apprenticeshipindia.gov.in'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;
